# Global working preferences

<!-- Generated by ~/.claude/commands/.codex/sync.sh from this header (commands/.codex/AGENTS.codex-extra)
plus ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md minus its claude-only blocks. Edit those sources, never this file. -->

## Codex specifics

- Never run `rm -rf ~/.agents`, recursively delete it, or remove its contents as cleanup. `~/.agents/skills`
  is the canonical skills library and `~/.codex/skills` stays a symlink to it; replacing a symlink never
  deletes its target. `~/.agents/skills/frontend-verify` stays a symlink to the live `~/Developer/todo/Automated_QA` repo.
- Preserve `~/skills-backup-20260916.tar.gz`. Before changing sync machinery, make a separate timestamped backup.
- `start`, `wrap`, `mission` and `refute-pr` are generated from `~/.claude/commands/<name>.md` into
  `~/.codex/prompts/` and `~/.agents/skills/<name>/`. The other prompts link into Automated_QA. Edit the sources.
- Model names below map to your own tiers: haiku = cheapest, sonnet = mid, opus = strongest.
- Never `sleep` to wait or chain `cd X && cmd`; use absolute paths and `git -C`.
- Read repository instructions and existing changes before editing; preserve unrelated user work.
  Resolve routine, reversible choices yourself; ask only when essential intent or authorization is missing.
- Never force-push, discard user work, send messages to people, merge, publish or deploy without authorization.
- Final responses state what changed, how it was verified, and what is unresolved. Keep credentials out of logs and commits.

